{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend\/alter"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bend-alter element indicates the number of semitones in the bend, similar to the alter element. As with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the alter element, numbers like 0.5 can be used to indicate microtones. Negative values indicate pre-bends or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"releases. The pre-bend and release elements are used to distinguish what is intended. Because the bend-alter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element represents the number of steps in the bend, a release after a bend has a negative bend-alter value,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a zero value."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"alter"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSemitones","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSemitones","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLSemitonesa"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<bend-alter>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property","title":"alter","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"alter"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSemitones","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLSemitonesa"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLBendV5alterSdvp"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbend\/alter"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBend":{"title":"MXLBend","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBend"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The bend type is used in guitar notation and tablature. A single note with a bend and release will contain two","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"bend elements: the first to represent the bend and the second to represent the release. The shape attribute","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distinguishes between the angled bend symbols commonly used in standard notation and the curved bend symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"commonly used in both tablature and standard notation.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBend"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbend"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBend/alter":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bend-alter element indicates the number of semitones in the bend, similar to the alter element. As with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the alter element, numbers like 0.5 can be used to indicate microtones. Negative values indicate pre-bends or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"releases. The pre-bend and release elements are used to distinguish what is intended. Because the bend-alter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element represents the number of steps in the bend, a release after a bend has a negative bend-alter value,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a zero value."}],"title":"alter","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbend\/alter","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"alter","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSemitones","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLSemitonesa","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend\/alter"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSemitones":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The semitones type is a number representing semitones, used for chromatic alteration. A value of -1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corresponds to a flat and a value of 1 to a sharp. Decimal values like 0.5 (quarter tone sharp) are used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"microtones."}],"title":"MXLSemitones","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsemitones","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSemitones"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSemitones","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSemitones"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"}}}